<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ducetius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 440 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ducetius was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicels">Sicels</a>, the native people of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, who around 460 BCE united most Sicel communities in a league against the Greek cities. He founded new towns, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morgantina">Morgantina</a> and challenged Syracuse and Acragas, but was defeated in 450 BCE and exiled to Corinth. He returned to found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kale-akte">Kale Akte</a> on the north coast and died around 440 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ducetius.jpg" alt="Ducetius" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giuseppe Emanuele Ortolani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ducetius.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
